 "youtube": {
  "title": "Battle of Myeongnyang: How Did 13 Ships Beat 133?",
  "description": "Battle of Myeongnyang, 1597: Admiral Yi Sun-sin had 13 warships. Japan came with about 133. How did he win without losing a single ship?\n\nJapan had just wiped out Korea's navy while Yi was demoted to a common soldier. The king told him to give up the sea and fight on land, but Yi wrote back: \"I still have twelve ships.\" He waited in the Myeongnyang Strait, a narrow channel where the tide roars like a river. When the current turned, the crowded Japanese fleet drifted back into itself, and about thirty Japanese ships were lost.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a true story like this every day. Would you have trusted the tide like Admiral Yi? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #myeongnyang #yisunsin #stickstory",
